From 87a53a94de9bd45e29f6166179ca2f21fc6f1778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:33:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix missing <algorithm> include in VectorExtensions.h

Vector::IndexOf() uses std::find/std::distance but only included
<type_traits> and <vector>. This compiles on MSVC because <vector>
transitively drags in <algorithm> there, but fails on GCC/libstdc++
(e.g. GCC 13 on Linux) with:

  error: no matching function for call to 'find(...)'

since only an unrelated std::find overload from <streambuf_iterator.h>
(pulled in via <fstream>) is visible without an explicit include.
---
 include/extensions/VectorExtensions.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/extensions/VectorExtensions.h b/include/extensions/VectorExtensions.h
index 79db094..2e178bb 100644
--- a/include/extensions/VectorExtensions.h
+++ b/include/extensions/VectorExtensions.h
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #pragma once
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <type_traits>
 #include <vector>
 
